      en: "Bodegas Salentein, in the Uco Valley, Mendoza, is an architectural gem that combines wine, art, and nature. The cross-shaped winery is not only designed for producing premium wines but also houses an important collection of Argentine and Dutch art in its cultural space, Killka. The vineyards extend to altitudes between 1,050 and 1,700 meters, benefiting from the exceptional conditions of the valley. Salentein was a pioneer in establishing the Uco Valley as a first-class wine region. A visit includes wine tastings, a tour of the impressive architecture, and the opportunity to enjoy the art exhibitions. The on-site Posada also offers luxury accommodation and a restaurant, making the visit a complete experience."
